                <div class="h-1 w-20 bg-amber-500 mx-auto mt-4 mb-3"></div>
                <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm max-w-2xl mx-auto">An ETP converts raw, harmful effluent into clean water through 4 standard, highly engineered processing stages:</p>
            </div>

            <!-- Steps Grid -->
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-8">
                <!-- Stage 1 -->
                <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-gray-200 flex flex-col justify-between relative">
                    <div class="absolute -top-4 -right-4 h-8 w-8 bg-amber-500 text-white font-extrabold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shadow">1</div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="h-12 w-12 rounded-full bg-gray-100 text-black flex items-center justify-center text-xl mb-4">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-filter"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h4 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-black mb-2">Stage 01: Primary</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            <strong>Physical Treatment:</strong> Screeners filter out large debris like plastic, cloth, and stones. An oil and grease trap removes floating lipids. It then enters an Equalization and Neutralization Tank to balance erratic chemical loads and pH.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest">Initial Screening & pH Balance</span>
                </div>

                <!-- Stage 2 -->
                <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-gray-200 flex flex-col justify-between relative">
                    <div class="absolute -top-4 -right-4 h-8 w-8 bg-amber-500 text-white font-extrabold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shadow">2</div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="h-12 w-12 rounded-full bg-gray-100 text-black flex items-center justify-center text-xl mb-4">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-bacteria"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h4 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-black mb-2">Stage 02: Secondary</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            <strong>Biological Treatment:</strong> Focuses on removing dissolved organic matters using microbes and oxygen in Aeration Tanks (MBBR, SBR, or ASP). Microorganisms naturally digest organic pollutants, forming sludge that settles in Clarifier tanks.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest">BOD & COD Biodegradation</span>
                </div>

                <!-- Stage 3 -->
                <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-gray-200 flex flex-col justify-between relative">
                    <div class="absolute -top-4 -right-4 h-8 w-8 bg-amber-500 text-white font-extrabold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shadow">3</div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="h-12 w-12 rounded-full bg-gray-100 text-black flex items-center justify-center text-xl mb-4">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-vials"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h4 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-black mb-2">Stage 03: Tertiary</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            <strong>Chemical & Physical Filtration:</strong> Fine particles and microbes are killed or removed via disinfection (Chlorination/Ozone) and passed through high-grade Pressure Sand Filters (PSF) and Activated Carbon Filters (ACF).
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-gray-400 uppercase tracking-widest">Odor, Color & Microbe Removal</span>
                </div>

                <!-- Stage 4 -->
                <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 shadow-sm border border-black flex flex-col justify-between relative">
                    <div class="absolute -top-4 -right-4 h-8 w-8 bg-black text-white font-extrabold rounded-full flex items-center justify-center shadow">4</div>
                    <div>
                        <div class="h-12 w-12 rounded-full bg-gray-100 text-black flex items-center justify-center text-xl mb-4">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-faucet-drip"></i>
                        </div>
                        <h4 class="text-lg font-extrabold text-black mb-2">Stage 04: Advanced (ZLD)</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-500 text-xs leading-relaxed mb-4">
                            <strong>Resource Recovery:</strong> Water goes through membrane filtrations (Ultrafiltration, Reverse Osmosis (RO)), ending at Multi-Effect Evaporators (MEE) to extract absolutely pure water for factory reuse, leaving zero liquid waste.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                    <span class="text-[10px] font-bold text-black uppercase tracking-widest">RO, UF & Zero Liquid Discharge</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

